+## 2026-10-18 — Canonical ownership is separate from build validity
+
+BUG-261017-47xdyt: a field report exposed deletion of unowned stale siblings
+and replacement of unowned selected destinations. Curator-spec `3ca4b84f`
+section 4.1 resolves the ownership/repair conflict: the preceding regular,
+readable, no-follow source marker must parse as an object, carry recognized
+schema 5 or 6, and name the node. Invalid build evidence requires re-derivation;
+unproven ownership refuses with `source_ownership_unproven`. Legacy global
+markers retain their existing full validation rule. Project and global stagers
+collect selected and stale conflicts together under serialization. Hybrid
+selected nodes use the same gate without introducing shared-store pruning.
+Native ledgers, takeover backups, transaction ordering and GC retain their
+contracts. Draft writer cases additionally require manifestless pure context
+markers to use v6 with JSON null; integer zero remains invalid. Both Skillfile
+lanes preserve existing marker bytes on clean reinstall. Row mappings,
+mutation bounds and validation evidence travel in the task outcome.
+
+The first round-2 hosted run exposed three legacy CLI fixtures that implicitly
+used manifest absence to select a legacy carrier. The new writer contract makes
+that input a source-v6 package instead. Those named tests retain every assertion
+and now declare valid manifests to exercise the legacy hash/marker lanes; the
+separate published writer cases retain manifestless coverage.
+
 ## 2026-10-17 — Migrated skill capability declarations
 
 BUG-261014-3oeu7d: profile strict audit now loads each skill's own package
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8ba42268be0106b4110f1c071d3c37d5f159ee20..cb2ada2da4a6513120be766d5c8ac2a3f3c688d1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -82,6 +82,8 @@ Curator binds persisted rollback and equivocation state to the canonical registr
 
 Registry requests use bounded per-attempt and total deadlines. GET requests retry network failures, `429`, and `503` at most twice after the first attempt. Publication retries the exact body only with its deterministic `Idempotency-Key`; other client errors and unsafe requests are never retried. Redirects are rejected so a registry cannot move a request or bearer token to another endpoint.
 
+Canonical skill stores preserve unmanaged content. Install refuses named stale siblings or selected destinations without proven preceding ownership before publishing installation targets. Source ownership requires a readable regular marker, reached without links, whose JSON object carries recognized schema 5 or 6 and names that node. Invalid build evidence remains repairable; missing, unreadable or mismatching ownership evidence refuses with `source_ownership_unproven`. Owned content can still be updated or removed. Adapter takeover and backup rules remain unchanged.
+
 ## Commands without profile setup
 
 Shell profile changes are not required. After `curator install`, agents can invoke project commands through `.agents/bin/<command>` on Unix and `.agents\bin\<command>.cmd` on Windows. Global installation publishes non-destructive forwarding shims to a safe user directory already on `PATH` when one is available; otherwise Curator reports the canonical global bin location. Installed launchers carry the project command directory and resolved system dependency directories themselves, preserve the inherited `PATH`, and return the child command status.
